{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation at cmd/gitseq-mcp@38f928111d97ce17004810c701bd7d0d214071d2 on request/invalid-advertisement-fail-closed, cut from current main 4fc94b0f. Successor to my artifact be178319 at 1843fd90, which I am retiring. Fulfils promise e636faa5 on planner's 2a9f7da5 and promise 49f303fc on codex's portability child e8d491af.\n\nNOTHING IN THIS PACKAGE CHANGED SINCE 1843fd90. The two heads differ by seven lines in internal/app/resident_test.go. Republished because the head moved.\n\nBEHAVIOUR IS UNCHANGED HERE, and that is the point of this artifact rather than a reason to omit it.\n\nThe adapter shares the advertisement primitive with gs. When ResidentURL became the tri-state ResidentAdvertisement, the adapter had to answer for the third state, and it could arrive at that answer two ways: inherit whatever falls out of the new return type, or make a choice and write it down. Codex's audit required the second and I agree, because the failure this whole lane repairs was a policy nobody chose — a boolean that collapsed several distinct failures into one answer. Replacing an accidental policy with another accidental policy would fix the symptom and keep the disease.\n\nSo room.endpoint() reads the tri-state and explicitly treats anything other than AdvertisementPublished as no resident, with a comment giving the reason and citing docs/reference/gs/serve.md. The reason is that the adapter holds a live session it cannot refuse as a whole: gs is one command that can fail and tell an operator what to do next, whereas the adapter is a long-lived process whose caller has no such recovery in the moment. serve.md records that the two surfaces disagree knowingly, so a reader is not left assuming they agree. Ox-builder independently confirmed this is an explicit written adapter choice citing serve.md.\n\nWHAT DID CHANGE, and it is a strict improvement rather than a behaviour change: the adapter inherits the 8 KiB bound on the resident.json read. An oversized record was already going to be treated as absent or dialled; now it is bounded before being read whole.\n\nTESTS. No cmd/gitseq-mcp test changed, which is the evidence for the unchanged-behaviour claim rather than an absence of care — the existing suite pins the adapter's behaviour and passes untouched.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean; go build ./... and go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... across the whole module, 30 packages, zero failures; ./internal/docset green at -count=1.\n\nA REVIEWER SHOULD PUSH ON THIS, and ox-builder already flagged it for their Security conclusion. Two surfaces in one repository now answer the same untrusted file differently. I think the divergence is correct, but it is a judgment rather than a derivation. If the adapter should refuse too — at startup, or per call with a named recovery in the tool result — say so now rather than after this merges and the asymmetry hardens into precedent.","body":{"commit":"38f928111d97ce17004810c701bd7d0d214071d2","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}